      "side": 1,
      "message": "Redundant duplicate check. `vlan_member` is assigned straight from `old_vlan` on line 273, so this block and the `if int(vlan_member) !\u003d int(vlan)` on line 280 test the identical condition: every mismatched port logs two messages (\u0027not configured for vlanX\u0027 here, then \u0027appears to be a member of VLAN ... should be ...\u0027 below). On Arista, access/native VLAN *is* the membership, so the two-variable split that Juniper needs collapsed into one.\n\nTrigger: any `--verify-switch-conf`, and every `--validate-env` pass over a host with switch_config_applied false.\n\nFix: drop lines 277-278 and remove the `if not last_nic:` guard on the line-280 warning, so the single remaining branch reports the mismatch for the last-NIC/public-VLAN case too, once.",
