      "writtenOn": "2026-10-20T12:04:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Inconsistent failure convention in one class: `configure` treats any falsy return as failure (`if not result`), while `modify` (line 46) and `verify` (line 65) fail only on a literal `False`.\n\nImpact: a switch plugin returning `None` - which is exactly what JuniperSwitchPlugin.modify did before this patch - is fatal for a move but silently counted as success for modify/verify. The next external switch plugin gets to guess which convention applies.\n\nFix: pick one. If the intent is fail-closed everywhere, use `if result is not True:` in all four methods (modify/verify/ls_config included) and state it in the SwitchPlugin docstrings.",
      "revId": "9c1dca9b874c856e390dea78c793f6bfb3ac97de",
